  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scoping study for the development of a Dutch Horti-Centre of the Future in North Sumatra, Indonesia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to develop a commercially, technically, environmentally, socially and financially sustainable business model for a Netherlands Horti-Centre of the Future (hereafter: the project), located in Humbang Hasundutan, North Sumatra, Indonesia.The project is connected to the North Sumatra Food Estate programme of the Government of Indonesia and is part of the combi-track Horti-Indonesia. This Centre of the Future will offer an easy and convenient way for Dutch companies, including service providers, to establish robust connections with the Indonesian market and display new technologies and methods in horticulture. It will also serve as a springboard for other regions in Indonesia and the ASEAN (Association of Southeast Asian Nations) region.</narrative>
  </description>
